711 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In smaller deployments, a basic approach involves configuring a Cinder Volume Node using LVM \(Logical Volume Manager\). This node typically resides on a local server with internal disks, turning it into a simple storage array. In this setup, only the Cinder Volume service runs on-premises, while the rest of the control services \(e.g., API, Scheduler\) remain centralized on the OpenStack Controller.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
